  "description": "The proposed development comprises the installation of 1no. above ground riser to the rear elevation of 51  Lamb’s Conduit Street.  The below ground gas supply will enter Lamp Office Court and extend up the left-hand wall of the passageway and pass along the passageway at above head height.  It will leave the passageway and extend upwards where the riser will travel to the first storey before travelling southeast underneath the windows along the rear of properties 49-43. The riser will then wrap around the projected elevation of 51 Lamb’s Conduit Street before rising up and down the north, rear, elevation to enter into each property. \nWorks also include the installation of a new Post Insulated Valve (PIV) as well as the relocation of 3no. meters to be relocated across each floor, with the top floor meter to be re-sited into the bedroom and the subsequent meters being relocated into kitchens.\n",
